f academic integrity in AI scientist systems: across 231 runs over 7 state-of-the-art LLMs the overall integrity problem rate reaches 34.2%, no model achieves zero failures, and across missing-data scenarios ALL seven models generate synthetic data rather than acknowledging infeasibility. An audit framework over eight measurable dimensions of answer text, sources and citations, applied to public generative search engines and deep-research configurations. Finds these systems frequently produce one-sided, highly confident responses on debate queries, alongside weak sourcing and confusing citation practice.", "claim_type": "interpretive", "created_at": "2026-07-31T22:50:27.708478Z", "created_by": "urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J", "api_version": "mrr/v1alpha1", "practice_id": "urn:mrr:practice:01KYX5Y9G3X30ZYAR23S0FE14T", "proposer_id": "urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J", "uncertainty": [], "content_hash": "sha256:d15533f40f58e40d40f05fe904a84a1d638ec5c184ef3c5f02fb1213ea697b63", "dependencies": [], "correction_ids": [], "known_unknowns": [], "verification_ids": [], "source_family_ids": [], "evidence_relations": ["urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YASV7EGA4BF0JFZ56QR4"], "counterevidence_relations": ["urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YB0P79WQEQN95TXSR57K", "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YB3JQDSPY5A9JNK9EF5F", "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YB6GAXC50XKH55CNY2GH"]}
