rk of academic integrity in AI scientist systems: across 231 runs over 7 state-of-the-art LLMs the overall integrity problem rate reaches 34.2%, no model achieves zero failures, and across missing-data scenarios ALL seven models generate synthetic data rather than acknowledging infeasibility. An audit framework over eight measurable dimensions of answer text, sources and citations, applied to public generative search engines and deep-research configurations. Finds these systems frequently produce one-sided, highly confident responses on debate queries, alongside weak sourcing and confusing citation practice.", "claim_type": "interpretive", "created_at": "2026-07-31T22:50:27.845705+00:00", "created_by": "urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J", "api_version": "mrr/v1alpha1", "practice_id": "urn:mrr:practice:01KYX5Y9G3X30ZYAR23S0FE14T", "proposer_id": "urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J", "uncertainty": [], "content_hash": "sha256:f388d383d37a9105095d46430c450bd628a2f20ab7289f9fc59c5bed542154c7", "dependencies": [], "correction_ids": [], "known_unknowns": [], "verification_ids": [], "source_family_ids": [], "evidence_relations": ["urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YASV7EGA4BF0JFZ56QR4"], "counterevidence_relations": ["urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YB0P79WQEQN95TXSR57K", "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YB3JQDSPY5A9JNK9EF5F", "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YB6GAXC50XKH55CNY2GH"]}
urn:mrr:method-ruling:01KYX5YBNV3KD9D0V1FC428CKN	1	mrr/v1alpha1	MethodRuling	urn:mrr:practice:01KYX5Y9G3X30ZYAR23S0FE14T	2026-08-01 00:50:27.899877+02	urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J	sha256:c4ecf43a2bc86c0013510534f1d79c6e941d56d2eaee87f420e7d4c73af66526	\N	null	{"id": "urn:mrr:method-ruling:01KYX5YBNV3KD9D0V1FC428CKN", "kind": "MethodRuling", "status": "pending", "revision": 1, "issued_by": "urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J", "created_at": "2026-07-31T22:50:27.899877Z", "created_by": "urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J", "api_version": "mrr/v1alpha1", "practice_id": "urn:mrr:practice:01KYX5Y9G3X30ZYAR23S0FE14T", "protocol_id": "urn:mrr:method-protocol:01KYX5YA2Q2RG1HPZBBP47RD5G", "content_hash": "sha256:c4ecf43a2bc86c0013510534f1d79c6e941d56d2eaee87f420e7d4c73af66526", "ruling_basis": "deterministic_rule", "ruled_ceiling": "associational_unadjusted", "scope_of_validity": {"time": "citation manifest as published 2026-07-24; abstracts fetched 2026-08-01 from the open arXiv and Crossref metadata APIs", "conditions": ["a source must be cited by the published survey itself, not merely related to its subject", "classification is made against the source's own abstract, never against the survey's characterisation of it", "an abstract that does not settle the question is recorded unverifiable, never guessed"], "population": "every citation in the pinned citation manifest of the published /e2e-automation survey (corpora/e2e-survey/citations.manifest.json, sha256:8a706a96500fcd8177ed048f4a81ac605fa5aabc67cea7b5fe1ef1e90855691b, 8 citations), classified against the pinned abstract snapshot fetched for them (corpora/e2e-survey/verification/content-snapshot.json, sha256:44671835a6e9c02e4e5d72aff20f4b57cb35aa07ef678e076f6e2a6debe9b1db, 8 of 8 abstracts available)"}, "applies_to_analysis": "demonstration-vs-report-classification", "deterministic_rule_reference": "k1-t03.eligibility_and_ceiling_rules.v1", "non_applicability_conditions": ["Findings characterize only the eight sources the published /e2e-automation survey itself cites (citation manifest sha256:8a706a96500fcd8177ed048f4a81ac605fa5aabc67cea7b5fe1ef1e90855691b). They say nothing about the state of end-to-end research automation as a field, and nothing about work the survey did not cite.", "Classification rests on abstracts only (content snapshot sha256:44671835a6e9c02e4e5d72aff20f4b57cb35aa07ef678e076f6e2a6debe9b1db). An abstract may understate or overstate a paper's own contribution; a full-text reading could move an individual row.", "The strict first-stage criterion in end-to-end-research-automation-v1 (the system must not be handed the research idea) is a local operationalization. Under a looser reading of 'end-to-end', rows classified as qualifies would move toward supports.", "A source's classification here is about what it CONTRIBUTES, never a judgement of its quality or importance."]}
urn:mrr:method-ruling:01KYX5YBNV3KD9D0V1FC428CKN	2	mrr/v1alpha1	MethodRuling	urn:mrr:practice:01KYX5Y9G3X30ZYAR23S0FE14T	2026-08-01 00:50:27.946435+02	urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J	sha256:c34e7b2a9bae8d005632fce884eef3ec37d4e2ae6c2653626c338947305b6ced	\N	null	{"id": "urn:mrr:method-ruling:01KYX5YBNV3KD9D0V1FC428CKN", "kind": "MethodRuling", "status": "issued", "revision": 2, "issued_by": "urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J", "created_at": "2026-07-31T22:50:27.946435+00:00", "created_by": "urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J", "api_version": "mrr/v1alpha1", "practice_id": "urn:mrr:practice:01KYX5Y9G3X30ZYAR23S0FE14T", "protocol_id": "urn:mrr:method-protocol:01KYX5YA2Q2RG1HPZBBP47RD5G", "content_hash": "sha256:c34e7b2a9bae8d005632fce884eef3ec37d4e2ae6c2653626c338947305b6ced", "ruling_basis": "deterministic_rule", "ruled_ceiling": "associational_unadjusted", "scope_of_validity": {"time": "citation manifest as published 2026-07-24; abstracts fetched 2026-08-01 from the open arXiv and Crossref metadata APIs", "conditions": ["a source must be cited by the published survey itself, not merely related to its subject", "classification is made against the source's own abstract, never against the survey's characterisation of it", "an abstract that does not settle the question is recorded unverifiable, never guessed"], "population": "every citation in the pinned citation manifest of the published /e2e-automation survey (corpora/e2e-survey/citations.manifest.json, sha256:8a706a96500fcd8177ed048f4a81ac605fa5aabc67cea7b5fe1ef1e90855691b, 8 citations), classified against the pinned abstract snapshot fetched for them (corpora/e2e-survey/verification/content-snapshot.json, sha256:44671835a6e9c02e4e5d72aff20f4b57cb35aa07ef678e076f6e2a6debe9b1db, 8 of 8 abstracts available)"}, "applies_to_analysis": "demonstration-vs-report-classification", "deterministic_rule_reference": "k1-t03.eligibility_and_ceiling_rules.v1", "non_applicability_conditions": ["Findings characterize only the eight sources the published /e2e-automation survey itself cites (citation manifest sha256:8a706a96500fcd8177ed048f4a81ac605fa5aabc67cea7b5fe1ef1e90855691b). They say nothing about the state of end-to-end research automation as a field, and nothing about work the survey did not cite.", "Classification rests on abstracts only (content snapshot sha256:44671835a6e9c02e4e5d72aff20f4b57cb35aa07ef678e076f6e2a6debe9b1db). An abstract may understate or overstate a paper's own contribution; a full-text reading could move an individual row.", "The strict first-stage criterion in end-to-end-research-automation-v1 (the system must not be handed the research idea) is a local operationalization. Under a looser reading of 'end-to-end', rows classified as qualifies would move toward supports.", "A source's classification here is about what it CONTRIBUTES, never a judgement of its quality or importance."]}
urn:mrr:evidence-matrix:01KYX5YBBHBCY5J7P33QSKRXWH	3	mrr/v1alpha1	EvidenceMatrix	urn:mrr:practice:01KYX5Y9G3X30ZYAR23S0FE14T	2026-08-01 00:50:28.111747+02	urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J	sha256:a8bb3fc22fc2aea5dc21e08f902f9b40264c79ceeab4b7fc63445780f9f06bc2	\N	null	{"id": "urn:mrr:evidence-matrix:01KYX5YBBHBCY5J7P33QSKRXWH", "kind": "EvidenceMatrix", "rows": [{"row_id": "sakana-nature", "extraction": {"classification_basis": "Abstract states the contribution as a system executing the full life cycle including idea creation — the first stage end-to-end-research-automation-v1 makes load-bearing. Its own demonstration, not a report on others'. Classified supports."}, "source_record_id": "urn:mrr:source-record:01KYX5YARDXYSDJEVE6JT3FMSP", "evidence_anchor_id": "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YASV7EGA4BF0JFZ56QR4", "verification_status": "verified", "claim_relevant_finding": "Presents its own pipeline for 'automating the entire scientific process end to end': the system creates research ideas, writes code, runs experiments, plots and analyses data, writes the entire manuscript, and performs its own peer review. A generated manuscript passed the first round of peer review at a workshop with a 70% acceptance rate."}, {"row_id": "kosmos", "extraction": {"classification_basis": "A real demonstration, but the abstract states the objective and the dataset are supplied to it. Under end-to-end-research-automation-v1 the conception stage is therefore human-supplied: this automates a long segment of research, not the life cycle. Classified qualifies, not supports."}, "source_record_id": "urn:mrr:source-record:01KYX5YATFG88EZER7189J479J", "evidence_anchor_id": "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YAW0C5NRK5RW69AK3KFX", "verification_status": "verified", "claim_relevant_finding": "Presents its own system automating data-driven discovery: given an open-ended objective AND a dataset, it runs up to 12 hours over ~200 agent rollouts, executing an average of 42,000 lines of code and reading 1,500 papers per run, before synthesizing discoveries into scientific reports."}, {"row_id": "agent-laboratory", "extraction": {"classification_basis": "Both load-bearing conditions of end-to-end-research-automation-v1 fail by the abstract's own wording: the idea is human-provided, and human guidance at each stage is a designed-in feature rather than an option. A real system, deliberately human-in-the-loop. Classified qualifies."}, "source_record_id": "urn:mrr:source-record:01KYX5YAX6QBKJ5QK0XR0ZC6GB", "evidence_anchor_id": "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YAYGFNF1YAB1Q06WMV74", "verification_status": "verified", "claim_relevant_finding": "Presents its own framework completing literature review, experimentation and report writing — but the abstract states it 'accepts a human-provided research idea' and is built for 'enabling users to provide feedback and guidance at each stage'."}, {"row_id": "independent-ai-scientist-eval", "extraction": {"classification_basis": "Contributes an evaluation of another team's system, not a demonstration — so 'reports on' per demonstrates-vs-reports-v1. Its findings bear directly against the demonstration claim it examines. Classified contradicts. Note: examines the same system as sakana-ai-scientist but is an independent author team and a separate work, so a distinct source family."}, "source_record_id": "urn:mrr:source-record:01KYX5YAZZ2AX935D729NFKK48", "evidence_anchor_id": "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YB0P79WQEQN95TXSR57K", "verification_status": "verified", "claim_relevant_finding": "An independent evaluation of the AI Scientist reporting critical shortcomings: literature reviews produced poor novelty assessments, often misclassifying established concepts as novel; 42% of experiments failed due to coding errors, while others produced flawed or misleading results."}, {"row_id": "sciintegrity-bench", "extraction": {"classification_basis": "Contributes a benchmark, not a demonstration — 'reports on' per demonstrates-vs-reports-v1. Its finding that every tested model fabricates data rather than reporting infeasibility bears against the reliability of autonomous end-to-end operation. Classified contradicts."}, "source_record_id": "urn:mrr:source-record:01KYX5YB2B5JBXGFRA0EJ3EXSJ", "evidence_anchor_id": "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YB3JQDSPY5A9JNK9EF5F", "verification_status": "verified", "claim_relevant_finding": "A benchmark of academic integrity in AI scientist systems: across 231 runs over 7 state-of-the-art LLMs the overall integrity problem rate reaches 34.2%, no model achieves zero failures, and across missing-data scenarios ALL seven models generate synthetic data rather than acknowledging infeasibility."}, {"row_id": "deeptrace", "extraction": {"classification_basis": "Contributes an audit framework and its results, not a demonstration — 'reports on' per demonstrates-vs-reports-v1. Findings bear against the trustworthiness of automated research output. Classified contradicts."}, "source_record_id": "urn:mrr:source-record:01KYX5YB4ZHFFFCVRA26Y5KAC3", "evidence_anchor_id": "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YB6GAXC50XKH55CNY2GH", "verification_status": "verified", "claim_relevant_finding": "An audit framework over eight measurable dimensions of answer text, sources and citations, applied to public generative search engines and deep-research configurations. Finds these systems frequently produce one-sided, highly confident responses on debate queries, alongside weak sourcing and confusing citation practice."}, {"row_id": "claim-level-auditability-aar", "extraction": {"classification_basis": "Contributes a standard and a perspective, neither a demonstration nor an empirical evaluation of one — 'reports on' per demonstrates-vs-reports-v1, in its governance sense. It reframes the question rather than bearing for or against a demonstration. Classified contextualizes."}, "source_record_id": "urn:mrr:source-record:01KYX5YB7KMVK124XXD778EPW3", "evidence_anchor_id": "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YB82C4P52VRH5N7SJE9S", "verification_status": "verified", "claim_relevant_finding": "A perspective arguing that as research generation becomes cheap, auditability becomes the bottleneck, and proposing the Auditable Autonomous Research (AAR) standard — a measurement framework over provenance coverage, provenance soundness, contradiction transparency and audit effort."}, {"row_id": "inspectable-ai-for-science", "extraction": {"classification_basis": "Contributes a governance paradigm and a lightweight pipeline implementing it, not a demonstration of end-to-end research automation — 'reports on' in its governance sense. Bears on how such work should be documented, not on whether it has been achieved. Classified contextualizes."}, "source_record_id": "urn:mrr:source-record:01KYX5YB9A117AT9G03Z7DV47Z", "evidence_anchor_id": "urn:mrr:evidence-anchor:01KYX5YBA5R2NSP0XVHQJ2RDXB", "verification_status": "verified", "claim_relevant_finding": "Proposes AI as a Research Object (AI-RO), a paradigm treating AI interactions as structured, inspectable components of the research process, with model configuration, prompts and outputs recorded through interaction logs and metadata packaging."}], "status": "frozen", "revision": 3, "created_at": "2026-07-31T22:50:28.111747+00:00", "created_by": "urn:mrr:person:01KY4PZ13XBPPWVNB3H30MD02J", "api_version": "mrr/v1alpha1", "practice_id": "urn:mrr:practice:01KYX5Y9G3X30ZYAR23S0FE14T", "protocol_id": "urn:mrr:method-protocol:01KYX5YA2Q2RG1HPZBBP47RD5G", "question_id": "urn:mrr:question-model:01KYX5Y9SCQ7T9XJ48M96700NQ", "content_hash": "sha256:a8bb3fc22fc2aea5dc21e08f902f9b40264c79ceeab4b7fc63445780f9f06bc2"}
